      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks for that. It's a good start/solid baseline. \n\nThe thing is, my boss just looked at the preliminary sentiment score for that draft and it's actually pretty low—like, it's flagging as \"neutral-to-negative\" because of words like \"disappointed\", \"fell short\", \"concerns\", and \"addressing concerns\". \n\nHe's worried that if the sentiment score is that low, the response might come across as too heavy or \"gloomy\" for a luxury brand. He wants us to brighten it up a bit so it feels more \"upbeat\" and \"positive\" while still apologizing. \n\nCould you try a version that's a bit more optimistic and focuses more on the \"wonderful\" experience we *want* to provide, rather than dwelling on the \"bad\" parts? Just please don't go overboard; I really don't want it to sound like we're ignoring the problem, but we definitely need that positivity score to move up.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
